      "content": "It is deeply painful to feel like the life you built has completely dissolved and that the world no longer sees you the way it once did. However, the *self* you are feeling lost is not the life that the world once saw, and the ability to help yourself is still within you. The \"end of the world\" feeling is a profound pain, and even in that pain, there is the potential to start carefully re-discovering what *you* are, independent of past external validation.",
      "source": "target",
